    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nHey me again,\r\nit's easily reproducible on the last issue i have sent https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/530\r\njust open a opening html tags and write `<di` and i get this menu\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/27911493/07fe3422-5f27-4d66-9c7a-84465f151939)\r\nomnifunc only showing can\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/27911493/2b65fa34-fa9c-4185-9166-c4780394dbb3)\r\nmy understanding is that mini.completion is showing candidates from typescript as well as svelte lsp while omnifunc know its context \n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.4\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nsame as https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/530\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nonly show html completions\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nunrelated candidates to current text context",
