            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> When do you press <C-x><C-o> to invoke 'omnifunc' (set to vim.lsp.omnifunc) in the original example? Is it after <di? If yes, could you try to press it after <?\r\n\r\nI get same result as omnifunc in that scenario\r\n\r\n> To see what list 'mini.completion' provides at certain points, set high delay (MiniCompletion.config.delay.completion = 1000000) and press <C-Space> after entering <, <d, and <di. If results are the same as with vim.lsp.omnifunc, then everything is fine.\r\n\r\nYes but that's not actually fine\r\n\r\nnow I'm closing this issue as it will be closed anyway by you as expected/by-design decision\r\nand i'm not trying to offend you in anyway you don't owe anyone anything\r\nthanks for your work!",
